  "explicit_limitations": [
    "Single model family: all primary runs use Claude Opus 4.7 via Vertex AI; generalization to Sonnet 4.7, GPT-5.5, Gemini 3.1 Pro, or open-source models is untested.",
    "Prompt-convention confounding: Li@Opus reproduces Li et al. (2025) Fig. 6 verbatim (bodyless method {:testEntry} plus runtime expect statements in Main()), which is not experimentally isolated from model capability or task difficulty.",
    "Architectural scope and blind spots of the ensures-binding gate: built for separated Spec.dfy / Impl.dfy pipelines; rejects meaningful inline postconditions without external symbol refs, and misses vacuous named tautologies like predicate P(x: int) { true } or {:axiom}/{:verify false} bypasses.",
    "Pre-launch VCG internal draft audit (~27% gate rejection across three Python benchmarks) is a reported structural rate requiring original per-component logs and sampling denominators for independent validation.",
    "Rust hidden-test B->C proxy (11.48% MBPP-Rust, 14.82% VeriContest LC) relies on trusted-toolchain and correct-oracle assumptions without per-failure disaggregation across transpiler, wrapper, implementation, or benchmark-oracle errors; VeriContest CF slice is left to future work.",
    "External VeriContest LC contrasts (7.79% VCG at 10 samples/prob vs. 5.51% GPT-5.5 and 1.88% single-shot Opus 4.7) are descriptive only due to unmatched sampling, repair, and harness budgets; Table 7 pass-rate gaps (-6.5 to -14.0 pp) are observational among self-selected outputs and non-causal."
